# m69v.ideal = m69u.ideal (w86) with R1' lever-held (its inputs removed; the lever is at (1,-3) under it).
# m69u.ideal: c78l's m69t (m69a turned into 9x6) re-timed by w86 for the s0 (4,2) / s1 (4,1) QC coupling:
# - open: s0's home pulls are LONG (>= 4 gt) and its first pull shares t2 with s1, so every coupled s1 firing is
#   a full push+pull (net zero) or its own pull; s0 carried to (3,2) is fed at (3,2,-1).
# - close: s0's first home spit also spits s1: TM -> (2,2) and TR -> (2,1) (TR takes MR's home); s0 carried pushes
#   TM home; MR goes (3,0) -> (3,1) (P3t) -> (3,2) (W pull) -> (2,2) by M0 pushing the LINE s0+MR, M0 pulls s0 back.
design designs/piston-door-3x3/tracks/s79/c69/m69v.txt
phase tile
open 0 use 1 -3 0
# bottom row down
open 2 set 0 -2 -1 minecraft:redstone_block
open 6 clear 0 -2 -1
open 2 set 2 -2 -1 minecraft:redstone_block
open 6 clear 2 -2 -1
